  "caption": "Quinn's knee started clicking and aching on the inner side of the kneecap, especially on stairs, at spin class and during long movies.\n\nMany knees have a plica, a soft fold in the joint lining. It's usually quiet, but lots of repetitive bending or a knock can irritate it, and it's often mistaken for other kneecap pain.\n\nWhat often helps: ease off repetitive bending for a while, build thigh and hip strength, check your bike saddle isn't too low, and give irritated tissue several weeks to settle. Painless clicking on its own is usually harmless.\n\nIf your knee locks, gives way, swells a lot, or isn't easing with rehab, get it assessed.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
